{"case_concurrency": 1, "case_id": "diagnosisarena:115", "dataset_id": "diagnosisarena", "dataset_selection_sha256": "d6975298f1cc1e66b3875c55b5694d4742d482e04e8d3dccd496533e5498e658", "dataset_snapshot_sha256": "bdf63ade2d1a892e9e3abe9d41c70cfbf62e414989a289dd8e319b339e66f2f5", "model_hash": "e5466c735d57bd3e32d4607a3e372b1862579edfef7864ca514e709a38853e26", "profile_id": "B2", "response": {"answer_text": "{\"answer\": \"C. Chemical burn from alkyl nitrite (poppers/Jungle Juice)\"}", "citations": [], "input_tokens": 10316, "latency_ms": 79296.008, "memory_mode": "off", "model_variant": "qwen3_8b_base", "output_tokens": 1621, "parsed_answer": "C", "provider_calls": 14, "reasoning_mode": "adaptive_mdt", "retrieval_mode": "off", "safety_flags": [], "system_profile": "B2", "tool_calls": 0, "trace_id": "harness-67ddead02a6947c384c3b835d2804d6b"}, "run_identity": "8e0e440bd0a891bea9dcd52fa2d9d8a9853997938e09c427564f3d0f0be9c164", "score": {"case_id": "diagnosisarena:115", "category": "unknown", "correct": false, "metric": "exact_choice_accuracy", "parse_success": true}, "source_revision": "64bb873fe651e1c71cd8b0958104dd911f042872", "trace_summary": {"mdt_activated": true, "mdt_complexity": "intermediate", "retrieval_calls": 0, "retrieved_documents": 0}}
{"case_concurrency": 1, "case_id": "diagnosisarena:116", "dataset_id": "diagnosisarena", "dataset_selection_sha256": "d6975298f1cc1e66b3875c55b5694d4742d482e04e8d3dccd496533e5498e658", "dataset_snapshot_sha256": "bdf63ade2d1a892e9e3abe9d41c70cfbf62e414989a289dd8e319b339e66f2f5", "model_hash": "e5466c735d57bd3e32d4607a3e372b1862579edfef7864ca514e709a38853e26", "profile_id": "B2", "response": {"answer_text": "```json\n{\n  \"single_choice\": \"B\"\n}\n```\n\n**Rationale:**  \nThe clinical presentation includes bilateral serous retinal detachments with no leakage on fluorescein angiography, normal choroidal vessels on ICG, and no evidence of vasculitis or inflammatory markers. These findings are consistent with **toxic choroidopathy** secondary to exposure to para-phenylenediamine, an aromatic amine found in some hair dyes. While other conditions like central serous chorioretinopathy (CSC) or Harada-like retinopathy may present with similar retinal detachments, the temporal association with hair dye exposure and the absence of typical features of CSC (e.g., leakage, pigment epithelium detachment) or Harada-like retinopathy (e.g., uveitis, serous retinal detachments with pigment epithelium detachment) support a toxic etiology. \"Retinopathy associated with the use of hair dye aromatic amines (RAHDAA)\" is a descriptive term, but the most specific and accurate diagnosis based on the findings is **toxic choroidopathy**.", "citations": [], "input_tokens": 1627, "latency_ms": 54046.741, "memory_mode": "off", "model_variant": "qwen3_8b_base", "output_tokens": 1132, "parsed_answer": "B", "provider_calls": 3, "reasoning_mode": "adaptive_mdt", "retrieval_mode": "off", "safety_flags": [], "system_profile": "B2", "tool_calls": 0, "trace_id": "harness-33b42eb232824dce94fea1693c329d4b"}, "run_identity": "8e0e440bd0a891bea9dcd52fa2d9d8a9853997938e09c427564f3d0f0be9c164", "score": {"case_id": "diagnosisarena:116", "category": "unknown", "correct": false, "metric": "exact_choice_accuracy", "parse_success": true}, "source_revision": "64bb873fe651e1c71cd8b0958104dd911f042872", "trace_summary": {"mdt_activated": false, "mdt_complexity": "basic", "retrieval_calls": 0, "retrieved_documents": 0}}
